.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_PACT_PIPELINE 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_pact_pipeline ,
.Nm dtfl_pact_exchange
.Nd parallelization contracts for operator inputs
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely.h
.Ft dtfl_pact
.Fn dtfl_pact_pipeline "void"
.Ft dtfl_pact
.Fn dtfl_pact_exchange "uint64_t (*route)(const void *, size_t, void *)" "void *ctx"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A parallelization contract describes how records reach an operator
input across the workers of a computation.
It is passed to
.Xr dtfl_op_builder_new 3 Ap s
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_input .
A pact never changes the number of records at a time, which progress
tracking relies on.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_pact_pipeline
keeps records on the worker that produced them: a direct, worker-local
connection.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_pact_exchange
routes each record to the worker
.Fa route Ns (record) modulo the number of peers, so records with the
same route value meet on one worker.
When
.Fa route
is
.Dv NULL
the record's type hash is used
.Pq Xr dtfl_type_hash 3 .
.Fa ctx
is passed to
.Fa route .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Both functions return a
.Vt dtfl_pact
value to pass to the builder.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
/* Keep data local. */
dtfl_op_builder_input(b, in, dtfl_pact_pipeline());

/* Route each record by a key hash across workers. */
dtfl_op_builder_input(b, in, dtfl_pact_exchange(route_by_key, NULL));
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
These functions do not fail.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_op_builder_new 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_scope 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_type_hash 3
.Sh HISTORY
These are the C forms of timely's
.Vt Pipeline
and
.Vt ExchangeCore
parallelization contracts
.Pq channels/pact.rs .
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
A
.Vt dtfl_pact
is a plain value created and consumed on the worker thread that builds
the operator.
The
.Fa route
function runs on the worker that produces each record.
